    "label": {
      "en": "rate for pension contributions"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tsceepi_rate"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "The employee's pension-insurance contribution rate (per 100), currently 8.72% of gross wages, the largest of the four employee contribution components in the Employee's Social Insurance Contributions table (pension 8.72%, sickness 1.99%, maternity 1.81%, health 6.98%, total 19.5%). It is combined with the (currently inapplicable) employer pension rate $tscerpi_rate to define the self-employed total pension rate $tscse_TotRate in ConstDef_lt, and is used directly in the tscct_lt ArithOp 'Pension contributions' formula, the tscee_lt UpLim parameter for the 'Pension' contribution ceiling, the tscer_lt BenCalc 'Pension' component, and both the tscse_admin_lt and tscse_lt self-employed pension-insurance formulas/components."
    },
    "explanation": {
